    {
      "id": "grammar-sugerir-que-subjunctive",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "sugerir que + verbo en forma especial",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that someone suggests that another person do an action?",
      "answerEn": "Use a form of sugerir, then que, then put the proposed action in the special subjunctive form.",
      "noteEn": "The subjunctive is a special verb form used here because the action is being proposed rather than stated as a fact. Each verb changes for its own doer: sugiere can introduce one person's suggestion, while the later verb changes for whoever would act. For example, ordinary hablamos becomes hablemos, and ordinary vemos becomes veamos.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Lucía sugiere que salgamos temprano.",
        "en": "Lucía suggests that we leave early."
      },
      "tags": [
        "grammar",
        "sugerir",
